    <md:uuid>35927f98-fae5-4d65-9a1a-36d2ebd43968</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<blockquote>
  <para>In questions 1 - 5, choose an equation of a line parallel to the given line and contains the given point. The choices are in slope-intercept form.</para>
</blockquote>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="909f5114-1beb-4172-83b5-3cfc322d081c"><problem><para>
      <para>Line \(y = 4x + 2\)
          Point
          \((1, 2)\) </para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(y=4x+2\)</para><para>\(y=4x-2\)</para><para>\(y=-\frac14x-2\)</para><para>\(y=-\frac14x+2\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(y=4x-2\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(y = 4 x -2\). </para>
      <para>The slope of a line parallel to \(y = 4x + 2\) is 4. The line contains the point (1,2).</para>
      <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS-->
      <para>\(\begin{aligned}y − y_1 &amp;= m(x − x_1)\\
        y − (2) &amp;= 4(x − (1))\\
        y − 2 &amp;= 4(x − 1)\\
        y − 2 &amp;= 4x − 4\\
        y &amp;= 4x − 2
        \end{aligned}\)</para>
      <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->

    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
